LWJGL-CI: library name overrides (`_glfw_*_library`) and glfwGetEGLConfig.

LWJGL-CI/glfw carries one commit, "LWJGL CI configuration", on top of upstream GLFW, and LWJGL
3.3.1's libglfw.dylib was built with it. This patch is the part of that commit that is compiled
on macOS. It adds four exported variables that LWJGL's Java side can set to point GLFW at a
specific EGL, OpenGL ES, OSMesa or Vulkan library, plus `glfwGetEGLConfig`. Without it our
library would lack 5 of the 137 functions and variables that the official LWJGL 3.3.1 build
exports (build.sh checks that the two export lists are identical).

The added and removed lines are exactly those of LWJGL-CI/glfw commit
c27b2d583412e9d4651f5ade755847ea81f94dcc (src/egl_context.c, src/osmesa_context.c,
src/vulkan.c), rebased onto 97da62a027794d9ff0f4512268cb9a73a8fb5073. Only the diff context
differs. LWJGL-CI rebases that commit onto every new upstream base, so the exact object used for
the 3.3.1 build in February 2022 is no longer reachable.

None of this code runs unless LWJGL is configured to use EGL, OSMesa or a custom Vulkan loader.
Minecraft does none of these.

